-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: see coa16-part19-general.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING and their comments).

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Part 19 -- Debentures: Supplementary provisions
-- =========================================================================================================

-- ---- s 749: Right of debenture holder to copy of deed ---------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9763 | 749 Right of debenture holder to copy of deed
-- src:9764 | (1) Any holder of debentures of a company is entitled, on request and on payment of such fee as may be prescribed, to be provided with a copy of any trust deed for securing the debentures.
-- src:9765 | (2) If default is made in complying with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:9766 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
-- src:9767 | (4) In the case of any such default the court may direct that the copy required be sent to the person requiring it.
@ref s 749 Right of debenture holder to copy of deed (src:9763-9767)
DECLARE `s 749 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 749 provide the debenture holder with a copy of the trust deed`

-- (1) "Any holder of debentures of a company is entitled, on request and on payment of such fee as may be prescribed,
-- to be provided with a copy of any trust deed for securing the debentures."  A claim of the holder against the
-- company; a grant limited by its own wording ("on request and on payment").
@ref s 749(1) Right of debenture holder to copy of deed (src:9764)
GIVEN `the person is a holder of debentures of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a trust deed for securing the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has made a request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has paid the fee that may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 749(1) the holder is entitled to be provided with a copy of the trust deed` MEANS
    IF       `the person is a holder of debentures of the company`
         AND `there is a trust deed for securing the debentures`
         AND `the person has made a request`
         AND `the person has paid the fee that may be prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any holder of debentures of a company is entitled, on request and on payment of such fee as may be prescribed, to be provided with a copy of any trust deed for securing the debentures"

-- The correlative duty of the company as a regulative rule: the text states no time.
@ref s 749(1) Right of debenture holder to copy of deed: the company's duty (src:9764-9765)
GIVEN `the holder has made a request and paid the fee that may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 749 act`
`s 749(1) the company must provide the holder with a copy of the trust deed` MEANS
    IF `the holder has made a request and paid the fee that may be prescribed`
    THEN PARTY Company
         MUST `s 749 provide the debenture holder with a copy of the trust deed`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (2) "If default is made in complying with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who
-- is in default."  The text names the officers in default and does not name the company itself (finding).
DECLARE `s 749(2) person` IS ONE OF
    `s 749(2) an officer of the company` HAS `s 749(2) the officer is in default (s 1121)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 749(2) another person`

@ref s 749(2) Right of debenture holder to copy of deed: the offence (src:9765)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 749` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 749(2) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 749(2) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 749`
    THEN
        CONSIDER person
        WHEN `s 749(2) an officer of the company` inDefault THEN
            CONSIDER inDefault
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is s 1121
        WHEN `s 749(2) another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names only the officers of the company who are in default, not the company
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section, an offence is committed by"

@ref s 749(3) Right of debenture holder to copy of deed: the penalty (src:9766)
`s 749(3) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- The gate is of the "in the case of" kind: listed in the name-test sweep (fork F34), not flipped, so JUST FALSE outside it.
@ref s 749(4) Right of debenture holder to copy of deed: the court's direction (src:9767)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 749` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 749(4) the court may direct that the copy required be sent to the person requiring it` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 749`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of any such default"

-- ---- s 751 comes first in this file because s 750(3) is "subject to section 751" -------------------------------

-- ---- s 751: Liability of trustees of debentures: saving for certain older provisions --------------------------

-- src:9779 | 751 Liability of trustees of debentures: saving for certain older provisions
-- src:9780 | (1) Section 750 (liability of trustees of debentures) does not operate—
-- src:9781 | (a) to invalidate any provision in force on the relevant date so long as any person—
-- src:9782 | (i) then entitled to the benefit of the provision, or
-- src:9783 | (ii) afterwards given the benefit of the provision under subsection (3) below,
-- src:9784 | remains a trustee of the deed in question, or
-- src:9785 | (b) to deprive any person of any exemption or right to be indemnified in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by him while any such provision was in force.
-- src:9786 | (2) The relevant date for this purpose is—
-- src:9787 | (a) 1st July 1948 in a case where section 192 of the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) applied immediately before the commencement of this section;
-- src:9788 | (b) 1st July 1961 in a case where Article 201 of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1032 (N.I. 6)) then applied.
-- src:9789 | (3) While any trustee of a trust deed remains entitled to the benefit of a provision saved by subsection (1) above the benefit of that provision may be given either—
-- src:9790 | (a) to all trustees of the deed, present and future, or
-- src:9791 | (b) to any named trustees or proposed trustees of it,
-- src:9792 | by a resolution passed by a majority of not less than 75% in value of the debenture holders present in person or, where proxies are permitted, by proxy at a meeting summoned for the purpose.
-- src:9793 | (4) A meeting for that purpose must be summoned in accordance with the provisions of the deed or, if the deed makes no provision for summoning meetings, in a manner approved by the court.
@ref s 751 Liability of trustees of debentures: saving for certain older provisions (src:9779-9793)
DECLARE `s 751(1) facts about an older provision` HAS
    `s 751(1)(a) the provision was in force on the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 751(1)(a)(i) a person then entitled to the benefit of the provision remains a trustee of the deed in question` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 751(1)(a)(ii) a person afterwards given the benefit of the provision under subsection (3) remains a trustee of the deed in question` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 751(1)(b) the exemption or right to be indemnified is in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by the person while any such provision was in force` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (1)(a) "Section 750 does not operate to invalidate any provision in force on the relevant date so long as any person
-- (i) then entitled to the benefit of the provision, or (ii) afterwards given the benefit of the provision under
-- subsection (3) below, remains a trustee of the deed in question."  "so long as" ends the saving when no such
-- person remains a trustee (fork F9).
@ref s 751(1) Liability of trustees of debentures: saving, paragraph (a) (src:9780-9784)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 751(1) facts about an older provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 751(1)(a) section 750 does not operate to invalidate the provision` MEANS
    IF facts's `s 751(1)(a) the provision was in force on the relevant date`
    THEN
        IF       facts's `s 751(1)(a)(i) a person then entitled to the benefit of the provision remains a trustee of the deed in question`
             OR  facts's `s 751(1)(a)(ii) a person afterwards given the benefit of the provision under subsection (3) remains a trustee of the deed in question`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "so long as any person (i) then entitled to the benefit of the provision, or (ii) afterwards given the benefit of the provision under subsection (3) below, remains a trustee of the deed in question"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any provision in force on the relevant date"

-- (1)(b) "Section 750 does not operate to deprive any person of any exemption or right to be indemnified in respect
-- of anything done or omitted to be done by him while any such provision was in force."
@ref s 751(1) Liability of trustees of debentures: saving, paragraph (b) (src:9785)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 751(1) facts about an older provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 751(1)(b) section 750 does not operate to deprive the person of an exemption or right to be indemnified` MEANS
    IF facts's `s 751(1)(b) the exemption or right to be indemnified is in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by the person while any such provision was in force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by him while any such provision was in force"

-- (2) "The relevant date for this purpose is (a) 1st July 1948 in a case where section 192 of the Companies Act 1985
-- applied immediately before the commencement of this section; (b) 1st July 1961 in a case where Article 201 of the
-- Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 then applied."  Which of the two applied is a fact (inputs).
@ref s 751(2) Liability of trustees of debentures: the relevant date (src:9786-9788)
GIVEN `section 192 of the Companies Act 1985 applied immediately before the commencement of this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Article 201 of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 then applied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 751(2) the relevant date` MEANS
    IF `section 192 of the Companies Act 1985 applied immediately before the commencement of this section` AND NOT (`Article 201 of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 then applied`)
    THEN JUST (Date 1 7 1948)
    ELSE IF `Article 201 of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 then applied` AND NOT (`section 192 of the Companies Act 1985 applied immediately before the commencement of this section`)
         THEN JUST (Date 1 7 1961)
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): neither case, or both cases, is not one the text provides for

-- (3) "While any trustee of a trust deed remains entitled to the benefit of a provision saved by subsection (1) the
-- benefit of that provision may be given either (a) to all trustees of the deed, present and future, or (b) to any
-- named trustees or proposed trustees of it, by a resolution passed by a majority of not less than 75% in value of the
-- debenture holders present in person or, where proxies are permitted, by proxy at a meeting summoned for the purpose."
-- The gate "While any trustee ... remains entitled" is of the "while" kind: listed in the name-test sweep (fork F35), not flipped, so
-- JUST FALSE once no trustee remains entitled; a vote or meeting that falls short of the terms is the grant's own limit: NOTHING.
@ref s 751(3) Liability of trustees of debentures: giving the benefit of a saved provision (src:9789-9792)
GIVEN `a trustee of the trust deed remains entitled to the benefit of a provision saved by subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefit is to be given to all trustees of the deed, present and future` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefit is to be given to named trustees or proposed trustees of the deed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proportion in value of the debenture holders present in person or, where proxies are permitted, by proxy who passed the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `the resolution was passed at a meeting summoned for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 751(3) the benefit of the saved provision may be given by resolution` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a trustee of the trust deed remains entitled to the benefit of a provision saved by subsection (1)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "While any trustee of a trust deed remains entitled to the benefit of a provision saved by subsection (1)"
    ELSE IF       (`the benefit is to be given to all trustees of the deed, present and future` OR `the benefit is to be given to named trustees or proposed trustees of the deed`)
              AND `the proportion in value of the debenture holders present in person or, where proxies are permitted, by proxy who passed the resolution` AT LEAST 0.75
              AND `the resolution was passed at a meeting summoned for the purpose`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "either (a) to all trustees of the deed, present and future, or (b) to any named trustees or proposed trustees of it, by a resolution passed by a majority of not less than 75% in value of the debenture holders present in person or, where proxies are permitted, by proxy at a meeting summoned for the purpose"

-- (4) "A meeting for that purpose must be summoned in accordance with the provisions of the deed or, if the deed
-- makes no provision for summoning meetings, in a manner approved by the court."
@ref s 751(4) Liability of trustees of debentures: summoning the meeting (src:9793)
GIVEN `the deed makes provision for summoning meetings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting was summoned in accordance with the provisions of the deed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting was summoned in a manner approved by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 751(4) the meeting was summoned as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the deed makes provision for summoning meetings`
    THEN
        IF `the meeting was summoned in accordance with the provisions of the deed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A meeting for that purpose must be summoned in accordance with the provisions of the deed"
    ELSE
        IF `the meeting was summoned in a manner approved by the court`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the deed makes no provision for summoning meetings, in a manner approved by the court"

-- ---- s 750: Liability of trustees of debentures -----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9768 | 750 Liability of trustees of debentures
-- src:9769 | (1) Any provision contained in—
-- src:9770 | (a) a trust deed for securing an issue of debentures, or
-- src:9771 | (b) any contract with the holders of debentures secured by a trust deed,
-- src:9772 | is void in so far as it would have the effect of exempting a trustee of the deed from, or indemnifying him against, liability for breach of trust where he fails to show the degree of care and diligence required of him as trustee, having regard to the provisions of the trust deed conferring on him any powers, authorities or discretions.
-- src:9773 | (2) Subsection (1) does not invalidate—
-- src:9774 | (a) a release otherwise validly given in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by a trustee before the giving of the release;
-- src:9775 | (b) any provision enabling such a release to be given—
-- src:9776 | (i) on being agreed to by a majority of not less than 75% in value of the debenture holders present and voting in person or, where proxies are permitted, by proxy at a meeting summoned for the purpose, and
-- src:9777 | (ii) either with respect to specific acts or omissions or on the trustee dying or ceasing to act.
-- src:9778 | (3) This section is subject to section 751 (saving for certain older provisions).
@ref s 750 Liability of trustees of debentures (src:9768-9778)
DECLARE `s 750(1) facts about the provision` HAS
    `s 750(1)(a) the provision is contained in a trust deed for securing an issue of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 750(1)(b) the provision is contained in a contract with the holders of debentures secured by a trust deed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 750(1) the provision would have the effect of exempting a trustee of the deed from, or indemnifying him against, liability for breach of trust` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 750(1) the trustee fails to show the degree of care and diligence required of him as trustee, having regard to the provisions of the trust deed conferring on him any powers, authorities or discretions` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (1) "Any provision contained in (a) a trust deed for securing an issue of debentures, or (b) any contract with the
-- holders of debentures secured by a trust deed, is void in so far as it would have the effect of exempting a trustee
-- of the deed from, or indemnifying him against, liability for breach of trust where he fails to show the degree of
-- care and diligence required of him as trustee ..."
@ref s 750(1) Liability of trustees of debentures: the void provision (src:9769-9772)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 750(1) facts about the provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 750(1) the provision is void in so far as it exempts or indemnifies the trustee` MEANS
    IF       (    facts's `s 750(1)(a) the provision is contained in a trust deed for securing an issue of debentures`
               OR facts's `s 750(1)(b) the provision is contained in a contract with the holders of debentures secured by a trust deed`)
         AND facts's `s 750(1) the provision would have the effect of exempting a trustee of the deed from, or indemnifying him against, liability for breach of trust`
         AND facts's `s 750(1) the trustee fails to show the degree of care and diligence required of him as trustee, having regard to the provisions of the trust deed conferring on him any powers, authorities or discretions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is void in so far as it would have the effect of exempting a trustee of the deed from, or indemnifying him against, liability for breach of trust where he fails to show the degree of care and diligence required of him as trustee"

DECLARE `s 750(2) facts about the release or provision` HAS
    `s 750(2)(a) it is a release otherwise validly given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 750(2)(a) it is in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by a trustee before the giving of the release` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 750(2)(b) it is a provision enabling such a release to be given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 750(2)(b)(i) the majority in value of the debenture holders present and voting that the provision requires` IS A NUMBER
    `s 750(2)(b)(i) the provision requires the vote to be taken at a meeting summoned for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 750(2)(b)(ii) the provision enables the release to be given with respect to specific acts or omissions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 750(2)(b)(ii) the provision enables the release to be given on the trustee dying or ceasing to act` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (2) "Subsection (1) does not invalidate (a) a release otherwise validly given in respect of anything done or omitted
-- to be done by a trustee before the giving of the release; (b) any provision enabling such a release to be given (i)
-- on being agreed to by a majority of not less than 75% in value of the debenture holders present and voting in person
-- or, where proxies are permitted, by proxy at a meeting summoned for the purpose, and (ii) either with respect to
-- specific acts or omissions or on the trustee dying or ceasing to act."  Not "not less than 75%": at least 0.75.
@ref s 750(2) Liability of trustees of debentures: what subsection (1) does not invalidate (src:9773-9777)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 750(2) facts about the release or provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 750(2) subsection (1) invalidates the release or the provision` MEANS
    IF       facts's `s 750(2)(a) it is a release otherwise validly given`
         AND facts's `s 750(2)(a) it is in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by a trustee before the giving of the release`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not invalidate— (a) a release otherwise validly given in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by a trustee before the giving of the release"
    ELSE IF       facts's `s 750(2)(b) it is a provision enabling such a release to be given`
              AND facts's `s 750(2)(b)(i) the majority in value of the debenture holders present and voting that the provision requires` AT LEAST 0.75
              AND facts's `s 750(2)(b)(i) the provision requires the vote to be taken at a meeting summoned for the purpose`
              AND (   facts's `s 750(2)(b)(ii) the provision enables the release to be given with respect to specific acts or omissions`
                   OR facts's `s 750(2)(b)(ii) the provision enables the release to be given on the trustee dying or ceasing to act`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not invalidate— (b) any provision enabling such a release to be given"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not invalidate" reaches only the release in (a) and the provision in (b)

-- (3) "This section is subject to section 751 (saving for certain older provisions)."  Section 750 as a whole: void
-- under (1) unless (2) or the section 751 saving takes the provision out.  JUST TRUE only where (1) applies and
-- neither (2) nor s 751(1) removes it.
@ref s 750(3) Liability of trustees of debentures: subject to section 751 (src:9778)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 750(1) facts about the provision`
      release IS A `s 750(2) facts about the release or provision`
      saving IS A `s 751(1) facts about an older provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 750(3) the provision is void, subject to subsection (2) and section 751` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 750(1) the provision is void in so far as it exempts or indemnifies the trustee` provision
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF       ((`s 750(2) subsection (1) invalidates the release or the provision` release) EQUALS (JUST FALSE))
            OR   ((`s 751(1)(a) section 750 does not operate to invalidate the provision` saving) EQUALS (JUST TRUE))
            OR   ((`s 751(1)(b) section 750 does not operate to deprive the person of an exemption or right to be indemnified` saving) EQUALS (JUST TRUE))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not invalidate" and "Section 750 does not operate to invalidate"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not reachable, s 750(1) answers JUST TRUE or NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 750(1) applies only "in so far as it would have the effect of exempting a trustee"

-- ---- s 752: Power to re-issue redeemed debentures ----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9794 | 752 Power to re-issue redeemed debentures
-- src:9795 | (1) Where a company has redeemed debentures previously issued, then unless—
-- src:9796 | (a) provision to the contrary (express or implied) is contained in the company's articles or in any contract made by the company, or
-- src:9797 | (b) the company has, by passing a resolution to that effect or by some other act, manifested its intention that the debentures shall be cancelled,
-- src:9798 | the company may re-issue the debentures, either by re-issuing the same debentures or by issuing new debentures in their place.
-- src:9799 | This subsection is deemed always to have had effect.
-- src:9800 | (2) On a re-issue of redeemed debentures the person entitled to the debentures has (and is deemed always to have had) the same priorities as if the debentures had never been redeemed.
-- src:9801 | (3) The re-issue of a debenture or the issue of another debenture in its place under this section is treated as the issue of a new debenture for the purposes of stamp duty.
-- src:9802 | It is not so treated for the purposes of any provision limiting the amount or number of debentures to be issued.
-- src:9803 | (4) A person lending money on the security of a debenture re-issued under this section which appears to be duly stamped may give the debenture in evidence in any proceedings for enforcing his security without payment of the stamp duty or any penalty in respect of it, unless he had notice (or, but for his negligence, might have discovered) that the debenture was not duly stamped.
-- src:9804 | In that case the company is liable to pay the proper stamp duty and penalty.
-- The gate "Where a company has redeemed debentures previously issued" is of the "where" kind: listed in the name-test sweep (fork F36),
-- not flipped, so JUST FALSE when it fails; the "unless" below is fork F10.
@ref s 752 Power to re-issue redeemed debentures (src:9794-9804)
GIVEN `the company has redeemed debentures previously issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provision to the contrary (express or implied) is contained in the company's articles or in any contract made by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has, by passing a resolution to that effect or by some other act, manifested its intention that the debentures shall be cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752(1) the company may re-issue the redeemed debentures` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company has redeemed debentures previously issued`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company has redeemed debentures previously issued"
    ELSE IF       `provision to the contrary (express or implied) is contained in the company's articles or in any contract made by the company`
               OR `the company has, by passing a resolution to that effect or by some other act, manifested its intention that the debentures shall be cancelled`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "then unless— (a) provision to the contrary (express or implied) is contained in the company's articles or in any contract made by the company, or (b) the company has, by passing a resolution to that effect or by some other act, manifested its intention that the debentures shall be cancelled"
         ELSE JUST TRUE -- by re-issuing the same debentures or by issuing new debentures in their place

-- "This subsection is deemed always to have had effect": the answer does not read the date of the redemption.
@ref s 752(1) Power to re-issue redeemed debentures: deemed always to have had effect (src:9799)
GIVEN `the date the debentures were redeemed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752(1) the subsection has effect for a redemption on the date` MEANS
    JUST TRUE -- the text: "This subsection is deemed always to have had effect"

-- (2) "On a re-issue of redeemed debentures the person entitled to the debentures has (and is deemed always to have
-- had) the same priorities as if the debentures had never been redeemed."
@ref s 752(2) Power to re-issue redeemed debentures: priorities (src:9800)
GIVEN `the redeemed debentures have been re-issued under section 752` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752(2) the person entitled has the same priorities as if the debentures had never been redeemed` MEANS
    IF `the redeemed debentures have been re-issued under section 752`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On a re-issue of redeemed debentures"

DECLARE `s 752(3) purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 752(3) stamp duty`
    `s 752(3) a provision limiting the amount or number of debentures to be issued`
    `s 752(3) another purpose`

-- (3) "The re-issue of a debenture or the issue of another debenture in its place under this section is treated as the
-- issue of a new debenture for the purposes of stamp duty.  It is not so treated for the purposes of any provision
-- limiting the amount or number of debentures to be issued."
@ref s 752(3) Power to re-issue redeemed debentures: new debenture or not (src:9801-9802)
GIVEN `the debenture is re-issued, or another debenture is issued in its place, under section 752` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `s 752(3) purpose`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752(3) the re-issue is treated as the issue of a new debenture` MEANS
    IF `the debenture is re-issued, or another debenture is issued in its place, under section 752`
    THEN
        CONSIDER purpose
        WHEN `s 752(3) stamp duty` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 752(3) a provision limiting the amount or number of debentures to be issued` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is not so treated for the purposes of any provision limiting the amount or number of debentures to be issued"
        WHEN `s 752(3) another purpose` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names only stamp duty and provisions limiting the amount or number of debentures
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "under this section"

-- (4) "A person lending money on the security of a debenture re-issued under this section which appears to be duly
-- stamped may give the debenture in evidence in any proceedings for enforcing his security without payment of the
-- stamp duty or any penalty in respect of it, unless he had notice (or, but for his negligence, might have
-- discovered) that the debenture was not duly stamped."  A grant: a failed condition outside the text's limit is not
-- covered; the "unless" met is the text's own no (fork F10).
@ref s 752(4) Power to re-issue redeemed debentures: the lender's evidence (src:9803)
GIVEN `the person lent money on the security of a debenture re-issued under section 752` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debenture appears to be duly stamped` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had notice that the debenture was not duly stamped` IS A BOOLEAN
      `but for his negligence the person might have discovered that the debenture was not duly stamped` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752(4) the lender may give the debenture in evidence without payment of the stamp duty or any penalty` MEANS
    IF `the person lent money on the security of a debenture re-issued under section 752` AND `the debenture appears to be duly stamped`
    THEN
        IF `the person had notice that the debenture was not duly stamped` OR `but for his negligence the person might have discovered that the debenture was not duly stamped`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless he had notice (or, but for his negligence, might have discovered) that the debenture was not duly stamped"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person lending money on the security of a debenture re-issued under this section which appears to be duly stamped"

-- "In that case the company is liable to pay the proper stamp duty and penalty."  "That case": the lender may give the
-- debenture in evidence without payment (fork F10).
@ref s 752(4) Power to re-issue redeemed debentures: the company's liability (src:9804)
GIVEN `the person lent money on the security of a debenture re-issued under section 752` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debenture appears to be duly stamped` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had notice that the debenture was not duly stamped` IS A BOOLEAN
      `but for his negligence the person might have discovered that the debenture was not duly stamped` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752(4) the company is liable to pay the proper stamp duty and penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 752(4) the lender may give the debenture in evidence without payment of the stamp duty or any penalty` `the person lent money on the security of a debenture re-issued under section 752` `the debenture appears to be duly stamped` `the person had notice that the debenture was not duly stamped` `but for his negligence the person might have discovered that the debenture was not duly stamped`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In that case"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In that case"

-- ---- s 753: Deposit of debentures to secure advances ----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9805 | 753 Deposit of debentures to secure advances
-- src:9806 | Where a company has deposited any of its debentures to secure advances from time to time on current account or otherwise, the debentures are not treated as redeemed by reason only of the company's account having ceased to be in debit while the debentures remained so deposited.
@ref s 753 Deposit of debentures to secure advances (src:9805-9806)
GIVEN `the company has deposited any of its debentures to secure advances from time to time on current account or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's account has ceased to be in debit while the debentures remained so deposited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753 the debentures are treated as redeemed by reason only that the account has ceased to be in debit` MEANS
    IF `the company has deposited any of its debentures to secure advances from time to time on current account or otherwise` AND `the company's account has ceased to be in debit while the debentures remained so deposited`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the debentures are not treated as redeemed by reason only of the company's account having ceased to be in debit while the debentures remained so deposited"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a company has deposited any of its debentures to secure advances from time to time on current account or otherwise"

-- ---- s 754: Priorities where debentures secured by floating charge --------------------------------------------------

-- src:9807 | 754 Priorities where debentures secured by floating charge
-- src:9808 | (1) This section applies where debentures of a company registered in England and Wales or Northern Ireland are secured by a charge that, as created, was a floating charge.
-- src:9809 | (2) If possession is taken, by or on behalf of the holders of the debentures, of any property comprised in or subject to the charge, and the company is not at that time in the course of being wound up, the company's preferential debts shall be paid out of assets coming to the hands of the persons taking possession in priority to any claims for principal or interest in respect of the debentures.
-- src:9810 | (3) “Preferential debts” means the categories of debts listed in Schedule 6 to the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or Schedule 4 to the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)).
-- src:9811 | For the purposes of those Schedules “the relevant date” is the date of possession being taken as mentioned in subsection (2).
-- src:9812 | (4) Payments under this section shall be recouped, as far as may be, out of the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors.
@ref s 754 Priorities where debentures secured by floating charge (src:9807-9812)
GIVEN `where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration`
      `debentures of the company are secured by a charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge, as created, was a floating charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 754(1) the section applies` MEANS
    IF       (    `where the company is registered` EQUALS `England and Wales`
               OR `where the company is registered` EQUALS `Northern Ireland`)
         AND `debentures of the company are secured by a charge`
         AND `the charge, as created, was a floating charge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where debentures of a company registered in England and Wales or Northern Ireland are secured by a charge that, as created, was a floating charge"

-- (2) "If possession is taken, by or on behalf of the holders of the debentures, of any property comprised in or
-- subject to the charge, and the company is not at that time in the course of being wound up, the company's
-- preferential debts shall be paid out of assets coming to the hands of the persons taking possession in priority to
-- any claims for principal or interest in respect of the debentures."
@ref s 754(2) Priorities where debentures secured by floating charge: the priority (src:9809)
GIVEN `where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration`
      `debentures of the company are secured by a charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge, as created, was a floating charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `possession is taken, by or on behalf of the holders of the debentures, of any property comprised in or subject to the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is at that time in the course of being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 754(2) the company's preferential debts are to be paid in priority to the claims on the debentures` MEANS
    IF       ((`s 754(1) the section applies` `where the company is registered` `debentures of the company are secured by a charge` `the charge, as created, was a floating charge`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE))
         AND `possession is taken, by or on behalf of the holders of the debentures, of any property comprised in or subject to the charge`
         AND NOT (`the company is at that time in the course of being wound up`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If possession is taken, by or on behalf of the holders of the debentures, of any property comprised in or subject to the charge, and the company is not at that time in the course of being wound up, the company's preferential debts shall be paid"

-- (3) "“Preferential debts” means the categories of debts listed in Schedule 6 to the Insolvency Act 1986 or Schedule 4
-- to the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989."  Both Schedules are outside the sources: whether a debt is in a
-- listed category is an input (the PLAN's "sch 4 [coa29]" is a false positive: that Schedule 4 is not this Act's).
@ref s 754(3) Priorities where debentures secured by floating charge: preferential debts (src:9810)
GIVEN `the debt is in a category listed in Schedule 6 to the Insolvency Act 1986 or Schedule 4 to the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 754(3) the debt is a preferential debt` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the debt is in a category listed in Schedule 6 to the Insolvency Act 1986 or Schedule 4 to the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Preferential debts” means the categories of debts listed in Schedule 6 to the Insolvency Act 1986 or Schedule 4 to the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989" (the borrowed Schedule's no, supplied as an input)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Schedules are not among the sources

-- "For the purposes of those Schedules “the relevant date” is the date of possession being taken as mentioned in
-- subsection (2)."
@ref s 754(3) Priorities where debentures secured by floating charge: the relevant date (src:9811)
GIVEN `the date possession is taken` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 754(3) the relevant date for those Schedules` MEANS
    `the date possession is taken`

-- (4) "Payments under this section shall be recouped, as far as may be, out of the assets of the company available for
-- payment of general creditors."
@ref s 754(4) Priorities where debentures secured by floating charge: recoupment (src:9812)
GIVEN `the payment was made under section 754` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 754(4) the payment is to be recouped out of the assets available for payment of general creditors` MEANS
    IF `the payment was made under section 754`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Payments under this section"
